# DTF tier manifest: catalog-backfill-liveness
#   (artifact-keeper#4168, #4191, #4305: 1.11.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + upstreams.mock-npm (the stdlib npm registry from
# virtual-member-gates, serving dtf-held 1.0.0 under any prefix).
#
# THE FIXES AND THEIR GATES (RED ak-backend:1.10.0, GREEN 1.11.0 and main)
# Each backfill case deletes the Go repo's `packages` rows and runs
# POST /api/v1/admin/packages/backfill, so what is asserted is what the
# backfill alone rebuilds (read back from packages/package_versions).
#   (CONTROL) a Go module version with only a .zip row is catalogued at the
#             zip's size, on every image.
#   #4191 Go `.mod`/`.info` (and Helm `.prov`) sidecar rows are no longer
#     backfill candidates. The catalog keeps the version row with the
#     smallest (checksum, size), so the oracle crafts a go.mod whose sha256
#     starts with 0 and a zip whose sha256 starts at 8 or above: a backfill
#     that considers the go.mod at all records its size, deterministically.
#     (FIX) v1.0.0 = the zip's size. 1.10.0: the go.mod's 48 bytes.
#   #4168 the walk skips quarantine_status quarantined/rejected rows.
#     (FIX) v2.0.0 quarantined and v3.0.0 rejected through
#     POST /api/v1/quarantine/{id}/quarantine|reject are absent from the
#     rebuilt catalog; v0.9.0 is present. 1.10.0: both are catalogued.
#   #4305 for the npm family a cached path without `/-/` is a packument.
#     (FIX) after fetching the dtf-held packument and tarball through an npm
#     Remote, GET /api/v1/repositories/{key}/artifacts?count=exact lists only
#     dtf-held/-/dtf-held-1.0.0.tgz with total 1. 1.10.0: also `dtf-held`,
#     total 2.
#
# NOT COVERED: #4169's Maven/Gradle backfill (already asserted by the wired
# migration-package-catalog and format-catalog-fixes tiers); the Helm .prov
# half of #4191 (same predicate, needs a provenance file); #4305's
# proxy-scans view.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-npm"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
